# Keeps the Docker build context (this repo) to just what an image needs —
# everything excluded here is either a build artifact regenerated elsewhere,
# or irrelevant to the build and multi-GB in a working tree.
#
# The re-includes below are for the root `Dockerfile`, which packages a build
# the host has already done rather than compiling in a stage. The idiom is
# exclude-then-re-include and order matters: the last pattern to match a path
# decides.

target/
node_modules/
dist/
data/
.git/
test-results/
playwright-report/
apps/web/e2e/.demo/

# Staged by `make container`: the stripped server binary and diesel-cli.
!target/container
# What the server serves and reads. Its writable siblings — assets, worlds,
# databases, config, modules — are volumes in `compose.app.yml`, so an image
# rebuild does not discard an instance's state.
!data/client
!data/packs
